1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,000
My father used to say: silence is not the absence of sound, but simply waiting for the right frequency.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
For forty years in this small room, he repaired more than just broken radios.

3
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:24,000
He reconnected the hopes, longings, and distant news of an entire neighborhood.

4
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:32,000
This radio was our family heirloom. Since my mother passed, it had not spoken a single word.

5
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Yet he never doubted. His fingers slowly turned through the frequencies...

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Searching through the hiss and crackle until the true voice was found.

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:56,000
And then, suddenly... the ancient melody of Tizita filled the room.

8
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:04,000
Sometimes what we repair is not merely an object, but the memory we shared.

9
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The frequency of memory never fades.

